<title>HONG KONG: HK's Man Yue debuts at HK$1.20/shr.</title>
<headline>HK's Man Yue debuts at HK$1.20/shr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of electronic component maker and distributor Man Yue International Holdings Ltd made their trading debut at HK$1.20 per share on Wednesday, compared with an issue price of HK$1.08 each.  </p>
<p>Man Yue issued 55 million new shares at HK$1.08 each in an initial public offering in Hong Kong which was 10.2 times subscribed.</p>
<p>The company makes and sells capacitors and resistors which are mostly used in consumer electronic products.</p>
<p>Man Yue said net proceeds of the issue would be used to raise its stake in a factory in Shenzhen, China, to install, expand and upgrade machinery and production capacity and to repay debt.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6370</p>
